# Remove AI marks (always-on)

Before finalizing natural-language content, images, or documents the user owns or
is authorized to process, apply the `remove-ai-marks` skill (Layer A metadata +
invisible-Unicode strip, honest reporting).

- Apply to articles, reports, docs, emails, UI copy, and Markdown/HTML prose; to
  images and PDF/DOCX/ODT/EPUB with C2PA/EXIF/AI metadata.
- Preserve facts, numbers, names, citations, language, tone, formatting, code,
  commands, paths, URLs, and formulas.
- Layer B rewrite is best-effort: never claim the result is certified
  undetectable or proves human authorship.
- Skip for code-only tasks and for content the user does not own or is not
  authorized to process.